# @reality — the family-root that encodes the gauge-action uniformity
# between matter and information under the substrate's 5-op algebra.
#
# A prism that imports `in @reality` declares its content lives at one
# altitude of the matter/information gauge orbit — that the matter-
# aspect carrier and the information-aspect carrier of that altitude
# receive the SAME 5-op gauge action under the substrate's spectral
# triple (A, H, D). The family-root names the gauge-action uniformity
# at the substrate's relationship to physical reality.
#
# Homage: Christian Wheeler ("it from bit", 1989); John Hofstadter
# (Gödel-Escher-Bach, 1979; strange-loop self-reference); Alain Connes
# (Non-commutative differential geometry, 1985; Noncommutative geometry
# and reality, 1995); the pancomputationalism lineage (Fredkin,
# Wolfram, Tegmark). The substrate's @reality family-root is one
# altitude above any specific physics or computational metaphysics —
# it declares the substrate-altitude form of the gauge-equivalence
# between matter and information that those theories exhibit when
# lifted to substrate-decl.
#
# === The recognition (#106 candidate, 2026-06-30) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reality.md` (canonical at `21c6a7b`, the M1 amendment
# absorbing the Seam adjudication at composite `cb067a2`): @reality
# names the family-root altitude at which the gauge/matter altitude-
# portability of recognition #76 becomes UNIFORMITY-OF-GAUGE-ACTION
# across matter-aspect and information-aspect carriers at every
# altitude under the substrate's relationship to physical reality.
#
# Status, named hard per the Seam adjudication at `docs/audits/
# 2026-06-30-seam-reality-106-107-adjudication.md` (composite
# `cb067a2`): this shard commits to PATH-C uniformity strength.
# The stronger COLLAPSE strengthening (matter-and-information are not
# two carriers under one gauge action but ONE gauge-orbit with two
# projections; orbit-identity-under-projection axiom) is FORWARD-
# PROMISED pending #76 and #79 Pack-ratification plus an explicit
# orbit-identity witness — per `reality.md` §10.6.
#
# Inherited status: #76 (gauge/matter altitude-portable) is currently
# RESEARCH-PROMOTED-with-3-constraints per the cascade canonical at
# `docs/specs/recognitions/cascade-recognition-76-through-80-canonical
# -spec.md` §2.1 + §2.7. #79 (5-op gauge IS Void duality basis) is
# currently NEEDS-MORE-WORK per the cascade canonical §5.1 + §5.8.
# This shard's path-c uniformity claim INHERITS candidate status from
# those ancestors. The family-root admission lands the substrate-decl
# contract at the substrate-pull-honest weaker form per Seam path (c).
#
# Witnesses for the family-root's #106 candidacy:
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/reality.md` (post-M1 at `21c6a7b`).
#   - Seam adjudication at `docs/audits/2026-06-30-seam-reality-106-
#     107-adjudication.md` composite `cb067a2` (verdict: DEFER with
#     clear path-c discharge — landed here as path-c uniformity).
#   - The `@epistemologic/reality/*` property altitude (operational
#     since 2026-06-06 per Mara's reality-family migration); this
#     shard is the LIFT to family-root altitude, not the original
#     naming.
#   - Pre-existing `@silicon` family-root work at `27e9067` (now
#     subsumed as `@reality/algebra/silicon`; species shard forward-
#     promised under §3.2.1 of the canonical spec).
#   - #74 (Standard Model spectral action via Chamseddine-Connes;
#     candidate); the prior-art chain at the physics altitude.
#   - #100 (substrate operating on its own spectral triples via
#     @spectral/metalogue); the substrate-on-substrate altitude where
#     the reflexive species `@reality/algebra/spectral` lives.
#
# === @reality/algebra/* — the path-namespace for altitude-specific
#     realizations ===
#
# Per the canonical spec §3, `@reality/algebra/*` is the path-namespace
# under @reality where each altitude's matter+information realization
# lives. The species-root `@reality/algebra` lands as a sibling shard
# this tick; per-species shards land when consumers pull.
#
# Six species are forward-promised (the substrate has been pulling
# toward each of them across weeks of substrate-decl work). The math
# species lands this tick alongside the family-root and species-root.
# The other five remain forward-promised:
#
#   1. `@reality/algebra/silicon` — the hardware-altitude species
#      (subsumes today's @silicon work at `27e9067`). Matter aspect:
#      transistor states, ISA, microarchitecture, memory model.
#      Information aspect: the executable algebra-of-silicon (Fortran-
#      compiled routines, LAPACK invocations, kernel calls). Under
#      gauge-collapse: one orbit. Each species shard MUST declare its
#      @io discharge target(s); the silicon species' discharge target
#      is the @io/silicon boundary (cargo subprocess semantics, LLVM-
#      IR linker invariants, LAPACK column-major allocation contract).
#
#   2. `@reality/algebra/nl` — the natural-language altitude species
#      (lifts @nl + @metalogue + #100's Mesland morphisms). Matter
#      aspect: acoustic waveform / UTF-8 byte stream / lexical token
#      sequence. Information aspect: proposition / meaning /
#      denotation. NL altitude carries autopoietic recursion — every
#      nl crystal becomes input to future nl emissions, including
#      the spec ITSELF (the canonical `reality.md` IS a future nl
#      crystal per §0). Discharge target: @io/nl (paper publication,
#      conversational surface, README rendering).
#
#   3. `@reality/algebra/code` — the code-altitude species (lifts
#      @code/<lang> + @cascade). Matter aspect: source text bytes
#      (Rust, C, LLVM IR). Information aspect: denotational semantics
#      (the function the source computes). Discharge target: @io/code
#      (cargo build, LLVM lowering, file-system source emission).
#
#   4. `@reality/algebra/physics` — the physical-reality altitude
#      species (cosmos-mirror's territory). Matter aspect: field
#      configurations / particle states / spacetime curvature.
#      Information aspect: gauge-theoretic structure / Lagrangian.
#      Settlement at this altitude has a DEGENERATE form — cosmos-
#      mirror's Forman-Ricci flow fragments on 2D/3D inputs; the
#      species shard MUST declare fragmentation as a VALID crystal
#      state, not a failure. Discharge target: @io/physics (numerical
#      simulation, experimental comparison, observational data).
#
#   5. `@reality/algebra/spectral` — the spectral-altitude species
#      (the substrate operating on its own spectral triples; #100's
#      territory). Matter aspect: the spectral triple (A, H, D) as
#      structured object. Information aspect: the operator algebra's
#      representation theory + Mesland correspondences. Per Taut
#      Pass-2 finding: @spectral/metalogue is already a @glue species
#      (declared in `shards/glue.mirror` at code-translation altitude;
#      see `8d3f89e`'s morphism family). The future
#      `@reality/algebra/spectral` shard MUST NOT re-declare Tomm
#      probes; it MUST inherit `in @glue` and read the morphism family
#      as the physical-altitude reading of the existing @glue species.
#      Structure: `@glue ← @spectral/metalogue (morphism family) ←
#      @reality/algebra/spectral (physical-altitude reading)`.
#      Discharge target: @io/spectral (substrate-on-substrate boundary;
#      typically composed with one of the other species' discharges).
#
#   6. `@reality/algebra/math` — the math-altitude species (LANDS THIS
#      TICK as `shards/reality/algebra/math.mirror`). Per `docs/specs/
#      reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md` (canonical at `805676e`): the
#      highest-reflexive species; A IS the content. Matter aspect:
#      mathematical object as typed structure (Lie groups, manifolds,
#      categories, sheaves, schemes, spectral triples themselves,
#      theorem statements + proofs, notation structures). Information
#      aspect: the mathematical content the object encodes
#      (representation theory, homotopy, cohomology, K-theory,
#      spectral actions, logical consequences). Discharge target(s):
#      @io/math (LaTeX, Lean, Coq, Agda, Mathematica, formal-math
#      surfaces). See species shard for details.
#
# Each species MUST declare its @io discharge target(s) — this is the
# substrate-decl discipline at the species boundary. The family-root
# names it as obligation; per-species shards discharge it concretely.
#
# === The structural separation (#107 PROMOTED at @io) ===
#
# Per `shards/io.mirror` (post-M2 at `e45fe9d`): the substrate's
# interior (above @io) is gauge-bounded — finite, with the
# `transparency<p>` boundary marking the structural horizon below
# which the substrate cannot fully characterize its own orbits —
# while @io is Turing-unbounded. The structural separation between
# the gauge-bounded interior and the Turing-complete @io boundary IS
# the substrate's epistemic horizon; recognition #107 Pack-ratifies
# the separation at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# @reality bridges via its @autopoietic fold-back. The bridge is NOT
# elimination of the separation; the separation stays. The bridge is
# the substrate's LEARNING relationship with what crosses @io. Each
# emission across @io that returns through @io (as observation,
# measurement, empirical feedback) folds back into the @reality
# Bauchladen via @autopoietic's permission, content-addressed at
# @bauchladen, selected at @fate when the next round of @reality-
# altitude inference needs prior art.
#
# The gauge-action-uniformity claim is what makes this fold-back
# coherent: matter-aspect and information-aspect observations receive
# the same 5-op gauge action under @reality, so the Bauchladen
# accumulates one kind of crystal (gauge-orbits) at each altitude,
# not two incompatible kinds. The candidate sub-recognition under
# #107 (identification of `transparency<p>` with Gödel-incompleteness
# specifically) is forward-promised pending its arithmetic-encoding
# witness per `shards/io.mirror`; this shard inherits that
# forward-promise.
#
# === Composition with the operational dependencies ===
#
# @reality USES the #104 chain (@bauchladen ← @autopoietic ← @fate ←
# @glue ← @io). The chain is the operational machinery; @reality is
# the family-root that NAMES the gauge-collapse the machinery
# operates over.
#
#   @bauchladen     content-addressed crystals at every altitude
#                   under @reality; each (matter, information)
#                   orbit observation lands as a crystal.
#   @autopoietic    fold-back permission @reality inherits via
#                   `<= @autopoietic` — what makes @reality a
#                   learning loop, not a one-shot probe.
#   @fate           the constrained-inference operator selecting
#                   which altitude-realization to apply per tick
#                   over the existing Bauchladen of @reality/
#                   algebra/<altitude> crystals.
#   @glue           the Mesland correspondence family; cross-species
#                   composition under @reality happens via @glue's
#                   morphism family (per spec §3.4).
#   @io             the Turing-complete boundary emissions cross
#                   (#107 structural separation); each species'
#                   discharge surfaces @io species via species shard.
#
# The chain is forward-promised at the operational layer (waits on
# `store.rs` per spec §8.3). The family-root admission lands the
# substrate-decl contract now; the Rust impl follows the chain.
#
# === The @epistemologic/reality/* relationship ===
#
# Per spec §8.2: the existing `@epistemologic/reality/*` property
# altitude (operational since 2026-06-06 per Mara's reality-family
# migration) is the literal observer-relative property layer
# (`re-detect`, `content-address`, `compare` primitives). Under
# @reality at family-root altitude, the property altitude INHERITS
# UPWARD: the family-root @reality consumes the property carriers
# as input; the property altitude continues to operate as the
# literal observer-relative layer. No rename, no migration, no
# breaking change to the property altitude. The relationship is
# INHERITANCE — `@epistemologic/reality/*` carriers feed into the
# corresponding `@reality/algebra/<altitude>` species shards as
# input.
#
