prism @reality <= @autopoietic {
  # Family-root for the gauge-action uniformity between matter and
  # information under the substrate's 5-op algebra. Lifts the
  # @epistemologic/reality/* property altitude (operational since
  # 2026-06-06) to a top-level @autopoietic family whose fold-back
  # permission, content-addressed at @bauchladen and selection-
  # operated by @fate, produces a Bauchladen of executable algebra-
  # of-reality crystals at each supported altitude.
  #
  # Under @reality at PATH-C strength, the 5-op gauge algebra ACTS
  # UNIFORMLY across matter-aspect and information-aspect carriers
  # at every altitude under @reality. The four invariances of
  # reality.md §2.5 (algebra closure, Hilbert linearity, Dirac
  # equivariance, spectral action invariance) discharge identically
  # regardless of which aspect label the carrier carries. The
  # stronger COLLAPSE / orbit-identity reading is forward-promised
  # pending #76 + #79 Pack-ratification and an explicit orbit-
  # identity witness — see `reality.md` §10.6.
  #
  # `@reality/algebra/*` is the path-namespace where each altitude's
  # matter+information realization lives. Six species are forward-
  # promised (silicon, nl, code, physics, spectral, math); the math
  # species lands this tick alongside the species-root.
  focus reality
  project reality
  split reality
  shift reality
  settle reality
}

# === The gauge_orbit carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one orbit
# under the @reality family-root's gauge action. Per the path-c
# uniformity reading (the substrate-pull-honest landing per Seam
# `cb067a2`): two carriers receive the same gauge action at one
# altitude; both projections land in the same gauge_orbit; the
# orbit is content-addressed by its altitude + the underlying
# H_altitude state's OID.
#
# Under the path-b COLLAPSE strengthening (forward-promised to
# `reality.md` §10.6 pending #76/#79 Pack-ratification + orbit-
# identity witness), matter_projection and information_projection
# would necessarily share an underlying OID; the family-root admits
# this strengthening as a future refinement without committing to
# it now.
#
# - `altitude`                 the substrate-ref naming the species
#                              under `@reality/algebra/*` whose
#                              gauge action this orbit sits under;
#                              one of {silicon, nl, code, physics,
#                              spectral, math, ...}.
# - `matter_projection`        the ref naming the matter-aspect
#                              projection at this altitude (e.g.,
#                              silicon transistor state, NL utterance
#                              bytes, source-text bytes, field
#                              configuration, spectral triple
#                              object, Lie group manifold).
# - `information_projection`   the ref naming the information-aspect
#                              projection at this altitude (e.g.,
#                              executable algebra, proposition,
#                              denotational semantics, Lagrangian,
#                              operator algebra representation, Lie
#                              group representation theory).
# - `gauge_action_witness`     the verdict witnessing that the 5-op
#                              gauge action discharges identically
#                              on matter_projection and
#                              information_projection at this
#                              altitude — the path-c uniformity
#                              claim's per-orbit discharge.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (altitude, matter_projection,
# information_projection). Two gauge_orbit records ARE the same
# orbit under content-addressing iff all three are byte-equal. The
# gauge_action_witness is the per-orbit verification of the
# uniformity claim; it does NOT participate in orbit identity.
type gauge_orbit = {
  altitude:               ref,
  matter_projection:      ref,
  information_projection: ref,
  gauge_action_witness:   verdict,
}

# === observe — register a gauge_orbit at a species altitude ===
#
# Given a species altitude ref + a matter-aspect projection ref + an
# information-aspect projection ref, returns the gauge_orbit for
# the registration. The species shard's witness predicate discharges
# the uniformity claim (four invariances of `reality.md` §2.5).
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same
# shape as @autopoietic.tick, @bauchladen.crystallize, @fate.roll
# (declarative obligation discharged at the species boundary).
observe(altitude: ref, matter: ref, information: ref) -> gauge_orbit { \ }

# === fold_back — return the orbit's content-addressed crystal to
#     the Bauchladen for future @fate consultation ===
#
# The @autopoietic discipline at @reality altitude: each registered
# orbit folds back into the @reality Bauchladen as a content-
# addressed crystal. The orbit's OID becomes its stable identity;
# future @fate inferences at the same or adjacent altitudes load
# the crystal as prior art.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary; the
# realisation MUST honor the autopoietic_closure_holds predicate
# the @autopoietic family imposes.
fold_back(o: gauge_orbit) -> oid { \ }

# === The bilateral requires obligations ===
#
# Downstream shards declare bilateral agreement (per recognition
# #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) with the @reality
# discipline by writing the obligations below.

# Per `reality.md` §2.5: the 5-op gauge algebra acts identically on
# matter_projection and information_projection of the same orbit.
# The four invariances (algebra closure, Hilbert linearity, Dirac
# equivariance, spectral action invariance) discharge identically
# regardless of aspect label. Inheritor shards (species under
# `@reality/algebra/*`) discharge per-altitude.
gauge_action_uniform(o: gauge_orbit) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `reality.md` §3.1: each species under `@reality/algebra/*`
# MUST declare its @io discharge target(s). The discipline at the
# species boundary: emissions cross @io through a species-specific
# discharge surface (LaTeX/Lean for math; cargo/LLVM for code;
# subprocess/FFI for silicon; numerical simulation for physics;
# substrate-on-substrate for spectral; conversational/paper for nl).
# Inheritor species shards discharge by naming their @io discharge
# species + a typed projection that wraps the crystal in @glass's
# `imperfect<discharge_outcome, io_surface, transparency(discharge)>`
# carrier.
io_discharge_declared(species: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Per `reality.md` §10.5 + Seam adjudication composite `cb067a2`:
# this shard's claims land at path-c uniformity strength. Path-c
# requires the four invariances of §2.5 + #76's altitude-portability
# (currently RESEARCH-PROMOTED-with-3-constraints). The stronger
# COLLAPSE / orbit-identity reading (path-b) requires the orbit-
# identity-under-projection axiom — NOT derivable from #76 + #79 by
# composition. Inheritor shards declare bilateral agreement that
# their claims sit at path-c; future shards may discharge a
# COLLAPSE-strength obligation when the §10.6 forward-promise
# closes (orbit-identity witness lands).
path_c_uniformity_held(o: gauge_orbit) -> verdict { \ }

# === The reality_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `reality_witnessing(o)` is the predicate consumer shards name in a
# `requires` clause to declare bilateral commitment (per recognition
# #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that the gauge_orbit
# `o` IS a valid @reality orbit — i.e., the orbit satisfies all
# three obligations above conjointly: gauge_action_uniform +
# io_discharge_declared (on the orbit's altitude species) +
# path_c_uniformity_held.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `autopoietic.autopoietic_closure_holds(prism)` (the prism-class
#     inheritance predicate this shard's family inherits via
#     `<= @autopoietic`).
#   - `bauchladen.bauchladen_witnessing(crystal)` (the crystal-altitude
#     inheritance predicate gauge_orbit crystals honor transitively
#     via @autopoietic's content-addressing).
#   - `fate.fate_witnessing(roll)` (the dice-roll inheritance predicate
#     species-shard @fate consultations discharge).
#   - `glue.glue_witnessing(c)` (the morphism-correspondence inheritance
#     predicate cross-species @glue translations discharge).
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
#   - `@reality/algebra` (THIS TICK; species-root): the path-namespace
#     prism that all six species inherit from.
#   - `@reality/algebra/math` (THIS TICK; first species): the math-
#     altitude species per `805676e`.
#   - `@reality/algebra/silicon` (forward-promised): the hardware-
#     altitude species subsuming today's @silicon work at `27e9067`.
#   - `@reality/algebra/nl` (forward-promised): the natural-language
#     altitude species lifting @nl + @metalogue + #100.
#   - `@reality/algebra/code` (forward-promised): the code-altitude
#     species lifting @code/<lang> + @cascade.
#   - `@reality/algebra/physics` (forward-promised): the physical-
#     reality altitude species (cosmos-mirror's territory); MUST
#     declare fragmentation as valid crystal state for degenerate
#     2D/3D Forman-Ricci settlement.
#   - `@reality/algebra/spectral` (forward-promised): the spectral-
#     altitude species; MUST inherit `in @glue` and treat
#     @spectral/metalogue as the morphism family rather than re-
#     declaring Tomm probes.
#
# No `requires reality_witnessing(...)` clauses are added at THIS
# shard. The family-root declares the predicate; consumers add the
# clauses when they pull. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] the
# species sub-shards follow when consumers pull.
reality_witnessing(o: gauge_orbit) -> verdict { \ }

out @reality
out gauge_orbit
out observe
out fold_back
out gauge_action_uniform
out io_discharge_declared
out path_c_uniformity_held
out reality_witnessing
